      "value": [
        {
          "resource_id": "monster_trait",
          "stats": {
            "trait_name": {
              "value": "Blinding"
            },
            "trait_description": {
              "value": "Breath 2A(concentrate, divine, necromancy, negative) The gholdako exhales a 60-foot cone of noxious breath that deals 7d8 negative damage (29 basic Reflex save). A creature that fails its save is also blinded until the end of its next turn (or for 1 minute on a critical failure) as a milky film coats its eyes. The gholdako can't use Blinding Breath again for 1d4 rounds."
            },
            "id": "ff32e670-efaa-49be-a0f2-c232692697f4",
            "updated_at": {
              "value": "2026-03-29T00:33:10.838404"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "resource_id": "monster_trait",
          "stats": {
            "trait_name": {
              "value": "Infectious Visions"
            },
            "trait_description": {
              "value": "(divine, enchantment, mental, poison)\n\nThe first time each round the gholdako damages a creature with a claw Strike, the creature must attempt a 27 Will save, as its mind is assaulted by horrifying visions. On a failure, the creature is confused until the end of its next turn. On a critical success, the creature is immune for 24 hours."
            },
            "id": "b459afa6-52cb-4753-a410-ff7112cee972",
